      "visual_action_start_seconds": 28.3,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.002833333333331467,
      "pause_after_samples": 196436,
      "pause_after_seconds": 4.092416666666667,
      "beat": "conditional-stakes",
      "visual_action": "A clearly hypothetical IF panel links a generic handedness-preference token to mirror-symmetry and preferred-axis question marks; no direction, sky sector, or outcome is chosen.",
      "display_citation": "Longo 2011 \u00b7 verbatim abstract \u00b7 conditional",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "i05l",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Longo reported: An unbinned analysis for a dipole component that made no prior assumptions for the dipole axis gives a dipole asymmetry of \u22120.0408\u00b10.011 with a probability of occurring by chance of 7.9\u00d710\u207b\u2074.",
      "word_count": 39,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/i05l-776d132d23c1.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "1426d8e48bf177b112f30cedb88078382dbba4c190e53ee1f3452ceccccbf150",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/i05l.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "54b83664d3807c31c0af1ea75a3685cfd0ebf0c3e98c2b11e2348de7388caae7",
      "audio_start_sample": 2048028,
      "audio_end_sample": 2801436,
      "audio_start_seconds": 42.66725,
      "audio_end_seconds": 58.36325,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 1280,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 42.666666666666664,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.0005833333333384871,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": "open-question",
      "visual_action": "An attributed Longo literature card presents the exact abstract sentence as another study's reported claim, with no axis geometry or adoption as this study's finding.",
      "display_citation": "Longo 2011 \u00b7 arXiv:1104.2815v1 \u00b7 verbatim abstract report",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "i05s",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Shamir reported: The results show that the local universe (z<0.3) is not isotropic in terms of galaxy spin, with probability P<5.8\u00d710\u207b\u2076 of such asymmetry to occur by chance.",
      "word_count": 34,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/i05s-c6ba0f9a82ec.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "bfb29ccdff8a881d1a2e100e5c0616dc5c79423b6a520199cf0e2c677cd8375c",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/i05s.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "b111ec0cb4a9479e0c150e61f03da6ad960a50f0fde77c2d26d2674bbe267451",
      "audio_start_sample": 2837436,
      "audio_end_sample": 3423804,
      "audio_start_seconds": 59.11325,
      "audio_end_seconds": 71.32925,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 1773,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 59.1,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.013249999999999318,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": "open-question",
      "visual_action": "An equal-weight attributed Shamir literature card presents the exact abstract sentence as another study's reported claim, with no preferred-direction geometry.",
      "display_citation": "Shamir 2012 \u00b7 arXiv:1207.5464v1 \u00b7 verbatim abstract report",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "i05d",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Land and colleagues reported: After establishing and correcting for a certain level of bias in our handedness results we find the winding sense of the galaxies to be consistent with statistical isotropy.",
      "word_count": 32,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/i05d-43f7a971b4e0.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "0ab844a0efa6729305750ff856891fa9395e38926af5fe3f75de61f3ab40be2c",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/i05d.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "f3f8631d13d1ec72c1ef784b7971447058ddc0fa6bc242047faf4469db1b4ca4",
      "audio_start_sample": 3459804,
      "audio_end_sample": 3973596,
      "audio_start_seconds": 72.07925,
      "audio_end_seconds": 82.78325,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 2162,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 72.06666666666666,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.012583333333338942,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": "open-question",
      "visual_action": "An equal-weight attributed Land literature card presents the exact abstract sentence as another study's bias-corrected null, without presenting it as settled truth.",
      "display_citation": "Land et al. 2008 \u00b7 arXiv:0803.3247v2 \u00b7 verbatim abstract report",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "i05u",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "These studies reported incompatible answers, so the literature remains disputed; this video adopts none of them as its finding.",
      "word_count": 19,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/i05u-5d5ed85e1f37.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "c46f44d48b428af27c12bcaff5271ea97908bbf781e0e2eba387e184c3661276",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/i05u.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "49614c41298ddd1e55b2f9ab36564808f3051bbc636440adf2de0346ab5ea87c",
      "audio_start_sample": 4009596,
      "audio_end_sample": 4370172,
      "audio_start_seconds": 83.53325,
      "audio_end_seconds": 91.04525,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 2506,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 83.53333333333333,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 8.333333333609971e-05,
      "pause_after_samples": 196435,
      "pause_after_seconds": 4.092395833333334,
      "beat": "open-question",
      "visual_action": "The three equal-weight attributed cards meet at a central DISPUTED AND UNSETTLED node; no card wins and no result geometry appears.",
      "display_citation": "Longo 2011 \u00b7 Shamir 2012 \u00b7 Land et al. 2008 \u00b7 claimed and disputed",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "i06",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "The catch is that people and algorithms can carry a left-right sorting bias, so the same images need a mirror control.",
      "word_count": 21,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/i06-b6ba11c74ba5.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "610a0607d0e038a117beeda9576dfba9b0558f8f278056d8d443c30a6f769987",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/i06.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "30f9822e07b536304cb8adfabcaed223137809ba79512cd1ffce2ac96ddb4c24",
      "audio_start_sample": 4566607,
      "audio_end_sample": 4906447,
      "audio_start_seconds": 95.13764583333334,
      "audio_end_seconds": 102.21764583333334,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 2854,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 95.13333333333334,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.004312499999997499,
      "pause_after_samples": 196435,
      "pause_after_seconds": 4.092395833333334,
      "beat": "catch-and-handoff",
      "visual_action": "A single conceptual galaxy image passes through human and algorithm labeling nodes, then moves toward a horizontal mirror plane that hands off to the existing method spine.",
      "display_citation": "Land et al. 2008 \u00b7 handedness classification bias",
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "section": "question",
      "text": "Can an apparent imbalance between clockwise and anticlockwise labels be separated from one introduced by the labeling process?",
      "word_count": 18,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s02-ee829c9ef24e.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "42fe4e520e2fd0a7ae0de25a7c1bc0dda2f72cd93976f6e63b4bd82ad535f874",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s02.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "b4962dc5d2918046c20bc6345cdbe34336b1d367a1d24ddf0e9a8a38c28b2d6d",
      "audio_start_sample": 5102882,
      "audio_end_sample": 5453090,
      "audio_start_seconds": 106.31004166666666,
      "audio_end_seconds": 113.60604166666667,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 3189,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 106.3,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.01004166666666606,
      "pause_after_samples": 196435,
      "pause_after_seconds": 4.092395833333334,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The technical question spans two equal, unresolved explanation lanes after the broad why-study introduction.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "Two explanations can create the same apparent imbalance.",
      "word_count": 8,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s03-2654139c78f3.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "87ef912035fd95327979b57f11fb15a9b0ba867248994bcd8f324dc57405c173",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s03.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "4d11eb1e01108c27c5ab5a45904b407364b95453788e8b1e27336e00f3c9c4ca",
      "audio_start_sample": 5649525,
      "audio_end_sample": 5829237,
      "audio_start_seconds": 117.6984375,
      "audio_end_seconds": 121.4424375,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 3531,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 117.7,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.0015625000000056843,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "Two explanation nodes feed the same unresolved count symbol.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "One places the pattern in the images.",
      "word_count": 7,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s04-c2f6b0727d04.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "0735f5db1d7dd967f689a6ec28639239bafc1b3aa8ffea913d961583ffaaaf9d",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s04.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "1b2ebf5f86c4a7791995d3a53a1e4e5b9ded75acba7916db453e0d057e53c8f5",
      "audio_start_sample": 5865237,
      "audio_end_sample": 6002325,
      "audio_start_seconds": 122.1924375,
      "audio_end_seconds": 125.0484375,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 3666,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 122.2,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.007562500000005912,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The IMAGE-LINKED lane illuminates around a spiral image.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "section": "two-worlds",
      "text": "The other places it in the labeling process.",
      "word_count": 8,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s05-798294462935.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "e25fa3d454cb7151d2cd76b20f5cc1c4a8edb39d26cc21b662cce3a1603b0c14",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s05.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "83c1c04bb38f193ed48ef43428c01b09cf4530e1712bc05f404080c5e7ee0d2a",
      "audio_start_sample": 6038325,
      "audio_end_sample": 6162741,
      "audio_start_seconds": 125.7984375,
      "audio_end_seconds": 128.3904375,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 3774,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 125.8,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.0015624999999914735,
      "pause_after_samples": 196435,
      "pause_after_seconds": 4.092395833333334,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The LABELING-PROCESS lane illuminates around a human-labeling node.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "Apply one decisive test to both worlds: mirror the same conceptual spiral horizontally.",
      "word_count": 13,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s06-ddb7198d6964.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "c019fccc6882eb9b319ae0915d758f4a56190ce3f42df7bd1461e9017a39076a",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s06.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "06b5a4c2cff06feaafe40da21fb893bd57f56d02390fdf0879fbb444518fc465",
      "audio_start_sample": 6359176,
      "audio_end_sample": 6657544,
      "audio_start_seconds": 132.48283333333333,
      "audio_end_seconds": 138.69883333333334,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 3974,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 132.46666666666667,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.016166666666663332,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "One conceptual spiral moves to a vertical mirror plane and begins a continuous horizontal flip.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "The geometry reverses, and its apparent label inverts from clockwise to anticlockwise.",
      "word_count": 12,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s07-4ec7573b3247.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "2f0b36c5d855d740a080394bbf93d51ab6c1faf38d21527157a2891333b9f8c8",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s07.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "4e17b05322a74fda1f0b2d3f854ef06409063dd63aa664e68ba323d0f2f5e939",
      "audio_start_sample": 6693544,
      "audio_end_sample": 6965416,
      "audio_start_seconds": 139.44883333333334,
      "audio_end_seconds": 145.11283333333333,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4183,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 139.43333333333334,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": -0.015500000000002956,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The same spiral completes its horizontal inversion while the label morphs from clockwise to anticlockwise.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "If the pattern belongs to the images themselves, it must follow that inversion.",
      "word_count": 13,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s08-b7adc8ea224c.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "e3b2d9a0ef43898a9bd119e76266b8c1204818e49c1890ab0426baca875cecb1",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s08.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "2da530b128c382b5b537302da18a7244c4bc6aa3c1ec755550aa522134fbae92",
      "audio_start_sample": 7001416,
      "audio_end_sample": 7193800,
      "audio_start_seconds": 145.86283333333333,
      "audio_end_seconds": 149.87083333333334,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4376,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 145.86666666666667,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.0038333333333469,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The image-linked prediction arrow follows the inverted geometry and pulses MUST INVERT.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "If it entered through the labeling process instead, it need not follow the pixels.",
      "word_count": 14,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s09-0de62cff2934.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "dacb1c93b393068a332219fcb02bc9bb0c9bc08e7217d1880ec3fbe66606897e",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s09.wav",
      "decoded_file_sha256": "7ad7c04bbeaea04f7ea84ea8c1d1e9f52fe50b0565ab214de283085b9f3e7128",
      "audio_start_sample": 7229800,
      "audio_end_sample": 7449832,
      "audio_start_seconds": 150.62083333333334,
      "audio_end_seconds": 155.20483333333334,
      "visual_action_start_frame": 4519,
      "visual_action_start_seconds": 150.63333333333333,
      "alignment_delta_seconds": 0.012499999999988631,
      "pause_after_samples": 36000,
      "pause_after_seconds": 0.75,
      "beat": null,
      "visual_action": "The labeling-process prediction separates from the pixel transform and pulses NEED NOT INVERT.",
      "display_citation": null,
      "timing_status": "PCM_DERIVED_FINAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "section": "mirror-climax",
      "text": "One mirror, two incompatible predicted behaviors: that difference is the scientific discriminant.",
      "word_count": 12,
      "raw_file": "audio_v5/raw/s10-3b19d3104719.mp3",
      "raw_file_sha256": "fa851a12f4e2102d58ec5c7f2bb4acabdd392abdf88208975ede181940f9df65",
      "decoded_file": "audio_v5/decoded/s10.wav",
